      "problem": "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle,$",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨2-4,\\,2\\sqrt{4},\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
